Essential Linux Commands for Every DevOps Engineer
 

🔹 𝐅𝐢𝐥𝐞 𝐒𝐲𝐬𝐭𝐞𝐦 𝐎𝐩𝐞𝐫𝐚𝐭𝐢𝐨𝐧𝐬
ls – List directory contents
cd – Change directory
mkdir – Create directories
rm – Remove files or directories

🔹 𝐅𝐢𝐥𝐞 𝐏𝐞𝐫𝐦𝐢𝐬𝐬𝐢𝐨𝐧𝐬
chmod – Change file permissions
chown – Change file owner and group
chgrp – Change group ownership

🔹 𝐏𝐫𝐨𝐜𝐞𝐬𝐬 𝐌𝐚𝐧𝐚𝐠𝐞𝐦𝐞𝐧𝐭
ps – Show running processes
kill – Terminate processes
top – Live process monitoring

🔹 𝐍𝐞𝐭𝐰𝐨𝐫𝐤𝐢𝐧𝐠
ifconfig – Network configuration
ping – Test network connectivity
netstat – Network statistics & connections

🔹 𝐒𝐲𝐬𝐭𝐞𝐦 𝐈𝐧𝐟𝐨
uname – Kernel/system information
hostname – Show/modify hostname
df – Check disk space

🔹 𝐏𝐚𝐜𝐤𝐚𝐠𝐞 𝐌𝐚𝐧𝐚𝐠𝐞𝐦𝐞𝐧𝐭
apt – Debian-based package manager
yum – RHEL/CentOS package manager
dpkg – Debian package tool

🔹 𝐒𝐡𝐞𝐥𝐥 𝐒𝐜𝐫𝐢𝐩𝐭𝐢𝐧𝐠
bash – Shell scripting
echo – Output text
grep – Search text using patterns

🔹 𝐔𝐬𝐞𝐫 & 𝐆𝐫𝐨𝐮𝐩 𝐌𝐚𝐧𝐚𝐠𝐞𝐦𝐞𝐧𝐭
useradd, userdel – Create/Delete users
passwd – Change user password

🔹 𝐅𝐢𝐥𝐞 𝐓𝐫𝐚𝐧𝐬𝐟𝐞𝐫
scp – Secure copy
rsync – Remote sync
wget – Download from web

🔹 𝐒𝐲𝐬𝐭𝐞𝐦 𝐒𝐞𝐫𝐯𝐢𝐜𝐞𝐬
systemctl – Manage systemd services
service – Legacy service handler
chkconfig – Enable/disable services
